description: A free, short, printable change-order form for handymen. What changes, the price, the new total and both signatures. No account needed.
heading: Change order for handymen
sub: A short form for when the customer asks for one more thing. Fill it in and get it signed before you start the extra work.
tips:
  - Write what you'll do, in plain words, and what it costs.
  - Add it to the price you already agreed and write the new total.
  - You and the customer sign and date it before the extra work starts. Leave them a copy or a photo of it.
  - Some states have their own rules for written approval. Check with your state licensing board.
